the census counts the copy's executions times its width, in its own context: true
nothing is staged where no node is: true
the term adds the filled bytes over the rate to the compute leg, exactly: true
a rate of None leaves both legs bitwise as without the term: true
a rate of 0 leaves both legs bitwise as without the term: true
no copy leaves both legs bitwise as without the term: true
the term never lowers the compute leg below the bound's: true
two nests, two copy contexts: true
a listing at rate L re-scores at R by stg * (1/R - 1/L), over every context: true
an outer [w < 4] and an inner [w < 2] admit 2 threads: true
an outer [w < 2] and an inner [w < 4] admit 2 threads: true
an outer [w < 4] and an inner [w < 2] report 6 refused workgroup threads as idle: true
an outer [w < 2] and an inner [w < 4] report 6 refused workgroup threads as idle: true
a Serial i < c guard on a staged copy reports no idle workgroup bytes: true
a Grid i < c guard on a staged copy reports no idle workgroup bytes: true
a Where fringe guard without a Workgroup If reports no idle workgroup bytes: true
mixed Serial and Workgroup guards charge idle lanes only for admitted serial steps (both orders): true
the staged-idle term adds filled idle bytes over the rate to the compute leg, exactly: true
staged_idle_rate None, 0, or empty idle copies leave both legs bitwise unchanged: true
model_staged_idle_rate value beats the backend's advisory staged_idle_rate: true
model_staged_idle_rate=none beats the backend's advisory staged_idle_rate: true
empty model_staged_idle_rate resolves to the backend's advisory staged_idle_rate: true
only the operand copy counts, at the iterations its index guard admits, in its own context: true
a kernel with a Tile_mma statement has no counted copies: true
a kernel with a Tile_mma statement has no counted idle copies: true
the tail is the continuous fill at B <= P: true
and at B = P: true
and at a saturated multiple of P: true
48 saturated blocks over 32 multiprocessors fill 3/4 under the tail, all of it without: true
unsaturated, the busiest multiprocessor's two blocks still fit its issue: no tail: true
64 blocks of 256 threads over 46 multiprocessors fill 32/46: true
the tail reaches the tile-MMA leg through the same fill: 48 one-lane blocks over 32, 4/3x: true
a plain reduction pays for each issued operand read of the same cell: true
a guard, a pointwise self-read and a packed operand each issue their own load: true
a mixed reduction charges the guarded copy once and each direct global read: true
both delivery paths add filled bytes over the same rate to compute alone: true
direct loads and staging copies with no rate leave both legs bitwise unchanged: true
the operand delivery census leaves Tile_mma kernels to their own rates: true
the auto gate (Ranked) is what derives the chain's plan here: true
the no-rate gate seeds both products of the chain: true
pricing both delivery paths keeps the two CUDA-shaped seeds: true
the actual gate's delivery charge separates the tied arithmetic: true
auto-legacy keeps the arithmetic tie and admits neither sketch: true
every staged leaf's census equals M*N*K*(BM+BN)/(BM*BN) cells of 4 bytes: true
a coalesced leaf is among them: true
every lowered 64x64x8/4x4 outproj leaf reports idle bytes equal to its staged bytes: true
every unguarded 4x4 outproj leaf reports zero idle bytes: true
